## Semantic hint injection — complete

**App:** ReVive marketplace (`WebTestBench_0023`), Vite + React + TS + shadcn/ui.

### Screens/components annotated (15 files)
`Header.tsx`, `SearchBar.tsx`, `SortDropdown.tsx`, `FilterSidebar.tsx`, `ProductCard.tsx`, `Index.tsx`, `ProductDetail.tsx`, `Login.tsx`, `Register.tsx`, `CreateListing.tsx`, `MyListings.tsx`, `Cart.tsx`, `About.tsx`, `Categories.tsx`, `NotFound.tsx` — every route and shared component in the app.

No prop-widening was needed: all shadcn/ui primitives already spread `{...props}` to their DOM root, so every `data-semtag-*` was added as a plain call-site JSX attribute.

### Id namespaces introduced
`nav.*` (header, incl. `.mobile` duplicates for the drawer), `browse.*` (search/sort/filters/grid, incl. `.item.<productId>`), `product.*` (detail page fields, gallery, message-seller dialog), `login.*` / `register.*`, `listing.*` (create-listing form, `.photos.item.<imageKey>`), `my-listings.*` (`.grid.item.<productId>`), `cart.*` (`.items.item.<productId>`), `about.start-browsing`, `categories.grid.item.<categoryValue>`, `not-found.home-link`.

Shared entities (`product.id`) are scoped per collection (`browse.grid.item.*` vs `cart.items.item.*` vs `my-listings.grid.item.*`) so no cross-collection collisions occur — verified via a cross-file grep of every literal `data-semtag-id` value (0 duplicates).

### Collections that couldn't be fully folded
- **ProductDetail gallery thumbnails**: only the container (`product.gallery.thumbnails`) is hinted as a collection; individual thumbnail buttons are left unhinted because they have no stable domain key, only an array index (folding them would require an `index-keyed-item` violation).
- **CreateListing sample photos**: solved with a derived stable key (`imageKey()`, the unsplash photo id parsed from the URL) instead of index — avoids the same problem.

### Deliberately left unhinted
Header search icon (duplicate of `nav.browse`), hero "Browse Items" anchor (in-page scroll, not real navigation), marketing stats section and all footers (static, non-interactive), Login demo-account helper text, `AlertDialogCancel` buttons (generic dismissal, low value).

### Known structural limitation (not fixed, out of scope)
`Index.tsx` renders `<FilterSidebar>` twice (responsive wrapper split), and each instance itself renders both desktop `<aside>` and mobile `<Sheet>` markup. This means filter-control ids are technically emitted twice over in the live DOM per breakpoint — mirroring a pre-existing native `id="upcycled"` duplication bug already in the app. Only one copy is visible at any given viewport (CSS `hidden`/`lg:hidden`), so runtime behavior for an agent driving the visible tree is unaffected. Fixing it would require a behavior-changing restructuring of `Index.tsx`, which is outside this task's constraints.

### Validation & checks
- `node scripts/validate-semtags.mjs src/` → **118 hinted elements, 74 files, 0 errors, 0 warnings**.
- Cross-file literal-id uniqueness grep → no collisions.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` → clean.
- `npm run build` → succeeds.
- `npm run lint` → 3 pre-existing errors / 8 pre-existing warnings, all in files never touched by this task (`components/ui/command.tsx`, `components/ui/textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`, plus fast-refresh warnings in various `ui/*` files) — confirmed via `grep` that none of those files contain any `data-semtag-*` content, so these are pre-existing boilerplate issues, not regressions.

